{{also|Poliomyelitis}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Poliomyelitis}}, from the {{der|en|grc|-}} {{af|grc|πολιός|t1=grey|μυελός|t2=marrow|-ῖτις|t3={{l|en|-itis}}|nocat=1}}. Compare {{cog|fr|poliomyélite}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|pŏ'lĭōmīəlīʹtĭs|pō'lĭōmīəlīʹtĭs}}, {{IPA|en|/ˌpɒlɪəʊmaɪəˈlaɪtɪs/|/ˈpəʊlɪəʊmaɪəˈlaɪtɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|poliomyelitides}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} Acute infection by the [[poliovirus]], especially of the [[motor neuron]]s in the [[spinal cord]] and [[brainstem]], leading to muscle weakness, [[paralysis]] and sometimes deformity.
#: {{syn|en|infantile paralysis|polio}}

